WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.502
In this video, you will plan a whole evening of lights.

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:09.596
You will save the places you like, put them in a sensible driving order, and send the route to your maps app.

00:00:09.596 --> 00:00:10.704
We start on the map.

00:00:11.606 --> 00:00:15.668
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:15.668 --> 00:00:17.793
That is the only address you need.

00:00:19.831 --> 00:00:22.109
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:25.655
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:25.655 --> 00:00:26.984
Tap Use my location.

00:00:26.984 --> 00:00:31.479
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.662
Your browser asks permission as well.

00:00:35.662 --> 00:00:36.360
Tap Allow.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:41.058
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:45.065 --> 00:00:46.165
Let's plan a night.

00:00:46.165 --> 00:00:48.144
First, choose what you want to see.

00:00:48.144 --> 00:00:49.353
Tap the season button.

00:00:51.731 --> 00:00:53.061
Pick the one you want.

00:00:53.061 --> 00:00:57.455
Christmas lights are the biggest, so tap Thanksgiving and Christmas Lights.

00:00:57.455 --> 00:01:00.925
Halloween, New Year, and other seasons are in the same list.

00:01:02.746 --> 00:01:06.446
When you see a place you want to visit, tap the heart on its card.

00:01:06.446 --> 00:01:08.048
That saves it to your night.

00:01:08.048 --> 00:01:08.655
Add a few.

00:01:08.655 --> 00:01:09.594
I will add three.

00:01:12.928 --> 00:01:13.997
Now tap My night.

00:01:13.997 --> 00:01:15.898
Your hearts are collected here.

00:01:15.898 --> 00:01:23.146
The stops are put in a sensible driving order, with the miles and the time between them, so you do not zigzag across town.

00:01:25.225 --> 00:01:27.443
When you are ready to go, tap Open route.

00:01:29.895 --> 00:01:36.036
Your maps app takes about nine stops at a time, so a long night is split into routes of nine or fewer.

00:01:36.036 --> 00:01:38.599
Each route starts where the last one ended.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.353
As you go, tick each stop when you have been there.

00:01:42.353 --> 00:01:48.332
That way, if you stop for dinner, or save the rest for another night, you can see exactly where you left off.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:55.665
Tap a route's button, and it opens in your maps app, ready for turn by turn directions.

00:01:55.665 --> 00:01:59.023
Choose Google Maps or Apple Maps, whichever you use.

00:01:59.023 --> 00:02:00.543
Then tap the X to close.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.049
Planning with family or friends?

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:06.133
Tap Share to send your night to them.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:08.765
They can open the same list on their own phone.

00:02:08.765 --> 00:02:11.178
You can also add the night to your calendar.

00:02:12.873 --> 00:02:14.943
Tap the heart on places you like.

00:02:14.943 --> 00:02:20.972
Open route splits your night into routes of nine or fewer, each starting where the last one ended.

00:02:20.972 --> 00:02:22.494
Tick off stops as you go.

00:02:23.896 --> 00:02:25.880
Next up: Weekly lights email.
